Title: Yellow Challenger
Credit: Written By
Author: MICHAEL GLASER-GARBRICK
Draft date: 10 August 2026
Revision: Rev 6 Psycho
Contact: mglaserg@gmail.com

/*


{{BW}}

{{RF}}

Big Bird

Nasa Engineer

Nasa Director
[[Setup]]
[[NE | RF(BW) | BB | RF | BW | RF | BB]]
{{BB = BIG BIRD}}
{{BW = BAD WOLF}}
{{RF = RED FOX}}
> Characters <


*/


INT. Challenger


{{RF}}
We're about to embark on the launch of the Challenger. This is a big day for America

{{BW}}
{{BW}} standing by

{{RF}}
{{RF}} standing by

{{BB}}
{{BB}} standing by


{{BW}}
I'm so happy that you could make it {{BB}}!

{{BB}}
I’m so happy I could be here with my best friends

{{RF}} spills coffee on himself

{{RF}}
Oh no this is worst thing that could happen on the Challenger

{{BW}}
This is like the Titanic of space shuttles

!They notice that {{BB}} has blue wires in his hands

{{RF}}
Hey what's that in your hand?

{{BB}}
Today’s is brought to you by the color blue!


!{{RF}} and {{BW}} realize this is an issue

{{BW}}
I'm sorry what?

{{RF}}
You’re holding wires in your hand are those important?

{{BB}}
Don’t ask questions you don’t want the answers to!

Feel the tension build

{{BB}}
Don't worry I'll hide it for you! I don't want you guys to get in trouble

{{RF}}
That's not it, it's -

{{BB}}
You know this reminds me of hide and seek with my friend Amelia Earhart. I couldn't find her, so I left!

{{RF}}
Wait you -

{{BW}}	
Oh god. Were you there with Amelia?! Where did you leave her?

{{BB}}
I said don’t ask questions you don’t want the answers to!

Take a beat

{{BB}} (CONT'D)
I am concerned about how you two are feeling. I want to make sure you two are happy

{{BW}}
I'm terrified. I want off this shuttle. I'm like a trapped animal right now

{{RF}}
I just want to see my children again

{{BB}}
Don't worry. I will be there for your children. Always

a beat passes

{{RF}}
(defeated)
I guess we have no choice but to continue with our mission

{{RF}} and {{BW}} start fumbling with controls. A rumble is felt

{{BB}}
Yay! We're going up like a balloon. You know, I remember a big balloon, the Hindenburg. I had so much fun with it, but then I popped it.

{{BW}}
Wait a minute-

{{RF}}
You were behind the Hindenburg?

{{BB}}
How many times do I have to tell you not to ask questions you don’t want the answer to?

The beat. Take it

{{BB}} (CONT'D)
I don’t like sad feelings and just want to see my friends smile!

{{BW}}	
I'm trapped! I'm trapped! {{RF}} he locked us into our seats!

{{RF}}
All I can think about is my family. I miss them so much. Where did I go wrong in life?

{{BW}} and {{RF}} start fumbling with their seats

{{BB}}
I’m bored guys!

{{BW}}
THEN LEAVE! PLEASE FOR THE LOVE OF GOD LEAVE


{{BB}}
The last time I was bored. I played tag at Tenerife! 

{{BW}}
(beat) 
When you say tag, do you mean two planes flew into each other?

{{BB}}
The other plane didn’t want to play tag, but I made them anyways!

{{BW}}
(beat) 
Oh my god. You are sick in the head you know that?!

{{BB}} breaks into a full psycho, I'm imagining a Walter White type

{{BB}}
You know you really are pissing me off with these questions. I was hoping we could be friends, but I see you are not interested. 

{{RF}}
Holy shit this is fucked. FUCKED!

{{RF}} starts tearing up

{{BW}}
I can still fight. I can still get us out of here! You son of a bitch! YOU FAT YELLOW SON OF A BITCH!

{{BW}} punches {{BB}} in the face

{{BB}}
(loses composure but becomes serious again)
Do you think that hurt my feelings?  You mistaken yourself that you are nothing more but playthings to me, mere puppets along for my ride. MY RIDE! Strung up by a sense of duty. But look at me (beat) there are no strings. This is nothing but a crack in my mask.

{{BB}} starts messing with the buttons

{{BB}}
The countdown has been started. 5 (beat) 4 (beat) 3 (beat)

{{RF}}
Oh god

{{BB}}
2 (beat)

{{BW}}
Goodbye

{{BB}}
1.

>**BLACK OUT**<



